meta {
  name: Get App
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/apps/{{appSlug}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Returns the full AppDetail for one app. Anonymous-friendly for published apps only.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Look up App by slug — 404 if not found.
    2. Non-published apps return 404 for anonymous callers (no auth, no visibility).
    3. When a current published AppVersion exists, enriches the response with manifest
       fields (display_name, categories, risk_class, license), chart_version, values_schema,
       installs count, auto_validation_state, and audit_approved flag.
    4. Returns AppDetail: all AppCard fields plus owning_organization_id, owning_user_id,
       github_installation_id, github_default_branch, repo_link_state, timestamps.

  Responses:
    200 OK        — AppDetail object; my_deployments lists the caller org's live deployments of the app ({ deployment_id, availability, url? }), [] for anonymous
    404 not_found — slug not found, or app is not published and caller is anonymous
}
